  "approvalChannelFinding": "Both approved families satisfy all twelve conditions of reviewRecordApproval — verdict, record verifier, independence, source binary, field map, classification hash, every artifact, provenance sidecar, visual evidence, no open correction, currency and asset identity. They are then refused by the clause the review-record channel shares with the overlay-profile channel: \"the field or anchor classification is not complete\". That clause reads classifiedFieldsOrAnchors and discoveredFieldsOrAnchors from field-classification.json, and the committed classification files carry classCounts and entries instead, so both values are undefined and the NaN comparison always refuses. This affects every family the gate can see, not only these four, and it is a property of the classification files rather than of this record. Measured, not inferred: with those two keys populated in a scratch copy (no repository path touched), both AK families return \"canonical independent-review record wave-c-final-a approved these exact bytes, and all twelve conditions hold\" through channel independent_review_record. Closing it needs one line in the classification generator, which this review lane does not own.",
